CSS Containment 2 layout and paint containment. 'contain' parses CSS's values (none, content, or any of layout, paint and
style; style containment scopes counters only and changes nothing here, size containment fails to parse). A contained
box is a stacking context and the containing block of its positioned descendants, and paint containment clips its
content to the padding box as 'clip: always' does.
